  "id": "infant-directed-speech",
  "term": "infant-directed speech",
  "definition": "Infant-directed speech is the way adults speak to babies, and it appears to provide an important environment for early language learning. It can include a distinct baby-like style with higher pitch, longer sounds, and smoother intonation, but it may also sound more like ordinary adult speech.",
